	comment "Conventional units that are neither base units nor defined by direct combination of base units are used in many application domains.  For example electronVolt for energy, feet and nautical miles for length.  In most cases there is a known, usually linear, conversion to a preferred unit which is either a base unit or derived by direct combination of base units.
